<title>USA: Maintenance cuts Friday hog kill at Indiana plant.</title>
<headline>Maintenance cuts Friday hog kill at Indiana plant.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>There will be no hog slaughter on Friday at Indiana Packers Corp (IPC) pork plant in Delphi, Ind., because of scheduled maintenance, a plant official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Every six months we have plant maintenance that takes us three days to perform so we perform it over a weekend and we cut out a Friday kill,&quot; said Ed Nelson, IPC vice president.</p>
<p>Nelson added that ham and pork belly processing would continue Friday and that slaughter would resume on Monday.</p>
<p>About 10,000 to 12,000 hogs are slaughtered per day at the Delphi plant, Nelson said.</p>
<p>((Bob Janis 312-983-7347))</p>
